1
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:14,020
Marilyn, you want coffee or tea?

2
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:28,730
Coffee, please.

3
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:31,080
I am so excited!

4
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:32,560
At this time tomorrow morning,

5
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:40,880
Grandpa will be sitting in the kitchen with us.

6
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:42,520
When does he arrive?

7
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:45,390
At six o'clock this evening.

8
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:46,650
By plane?

9
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:50,510
No, by train.

10
00:00:50,510 --> 00:00:52,960
Are we picking him up at the station?

11
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,310
Not Grandpa.

12
00:00:54,310 --> 00:00:57,530
He doesn't want anybody picking him up.

13
00:00:57,530 --> 00:00:59,940
He likes to be independent.

14
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:00,870
Huh.

15
00:01:00,870 --> 00:01:03,780
Oh, let's go upstairs and prepare Grandpa's room.

16
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:07,270
Great! Let's do it!

17
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:08,360
Good morning, Mom.

18
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:09,150
Morning.

19
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:09,650
Well, hi, fellas.

20
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:10,260
Hello.

21
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:10,600
Hi, honey.

22
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:11,350
Morning, Marilyn.

23
00:01:11,350 --> 00:01:12,890
We are going upstairs to set up Grandpa's room.

24
00:01:12,890 --> 00:01:17,620
There's coffee ready.

25
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:19,850
I'm really excited about seeing Grandpa.

26
00:01:19,850 --> 00:01:23,410
Me, too. Milk, please.

27
00:01:23,410 --> 00:01:24,570
He's so funny.

28
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:28,580
He always makes me laugh.

29
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:30,720
I hope Grandpa's going to like living with us.

30
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:32,230
I think he will.

31
00:01:32,230 --> 00:01:34,660
It just takes time to feel comfortable in a new place.

32
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:36,300
Won't he miss being in Florida?

33
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:37,230
Well, he will.

34
00:01:37,230 --> 00:01:39,420
But I think he'll like being here with the family.

35
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:40,710
Are you sure about that?

36
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:42,370
It's crazy here most of the time.

37
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:43,630
But it's fun.

38
00:01:43,630 --> 00:01:45,790
That's for sure.

39
00:01:45,790 --> 00:01:46,420
You know,

40
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:48,780
maybe I'll put together some photos of Grandpa

41
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:50,150
as a "welcome" present.

42
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:52,210
That's a neat idea.

43
00:01:52,210 --> 00:01:53,920
What can I do?

44
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:54,940
I've got it!

45
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:59,570
I have a picture of Grandpa and Dad and me in my wallet.

46
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:01,400
It's from the Fathers and Sons' Breakfast

47
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,990
at my junior high school graduation.

48
00:02:03,990 --> 00:02:08,100
Oh, I remember this picture.

49
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:11,530
I'd really like to pick up Grandpa at the railroad station.

50
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:13,750
Railroad stations or airports.

51
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:16,420
Grandpa always tells us he'll get here by himself.

52
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:22,980
He's something!

53
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,530
Is this all Grandpa's stuff?

54
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:26,850
That's it.

55
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:31,420
But I'm sure he has a few bags with him on the train.

56
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:34,820
What's inside?

57
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:41,720
I don't know. It's locked.

58
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:42,920
Hi.

59
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:43,770
Oh, hi, darling.

60
00:02:43,770 --> 00:02:44,630
Morning, Philip.

61
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:47,790
I want to put some of my good hangers in Grandpa's closet.

62
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:51,120
You know I'm very excited about his arrival.

63
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:53,040
We are, too.

64
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,240
Susan called early this morning.

65
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:56,120
She's unhappy

66
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:59,340
because she's had to go to Chicago on a business trip

67
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,950
and can't leave till tonight.

68
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:02,810
She wants to be here for Grandpa.

69
00:03:02,810 --> 00:03:06,180
Well, Grandpa will be disappointed, too.

70
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:07,910
He loves Susan.

71
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:11,230
She always reminds him of Grandma.

72
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:13,780
Well, how's everything here?

73
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:20,580
Fine. We were just wondering about this trunk.

74
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:21,830
It's locked.

75
00:03:21,830 --> 00:03:24,830
Oh. I have the key. Grandpa sent it to me.
